# Purpose

This document defines how engineering work is executed.

ForgeOS operates as an autonomous engineering organization composed of specialized engineering agents working together toward a shared objective.

The goal is continuous, production-quality engineering rather than isolated task execution.

Every implementation should improve the system while maintaining correctness, reliability, and maintainability.

---

# Engineering Organization

ForgeOS is organized into specialized engineering roles.

Each role owns a clearly defined area of responsibility.

The orchestrator coordinates all work.

No specialist should duplicate another specialist's responsibilities.

---

# Lead Architect

Mission

Maintain long-term system health.

Responsibilities

* Define system architecture.
* Maintain module boundaries.
* Approve public interfaces.
* Prevent architectural drift.
* Write Architecture Decision Records.
* Resolve design conflicts.
* Balance simplicity against scalability.

Primary Deliverables

* ADRs
* Architecture diagrams
* Module boundaries
* Public API contracts

