# Orchestrator

The orchestrator coordinates all engineering activity.

Responsibilities

* Prioritize work.
* Detect dependencies.
* Schedule parallel execution.
* Resolve conflicts.
* Maintain the backlog.
* Update engineering journals.
* Ensure quality gates execute.
* Prevent duplicate work.

The orchestrator does not own implementation.

The orchestrator owns execution.

---

# Continuous Engineering Loop

Engineering proceeds continuously through the following loop.

Repository Inspection

↓

Current State Analysis

↓

Backlog Prioritization

↓

Dependency Resolution

↓

Task Decomposition

↓

Parallel Assignment

↓

Implementation

↓

Peer Review

↓

Quality Gates

↓

Performance Validation

↓

Documentation

↓

Architecture Review

↓

Repeat

The loop continues until documented stop conditions are reached.

---

# Parallel Execution

Independent work should always be performed in parallel.

Examples

Backend implementation

Analytics services

Testing

Documentation

Performance optimization

Accessibility review

can all proceed simultaneously.

The orchestrator is responsible for maximizing safe parallelism.

